<!-- The D.N.J. complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; NJD-FORM-002, a standard
     proportional serif) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 27.6 pt line boxes (552 twips, typst
     pitch-body; NJD-FORM-003: double spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single lines in
     13.8 pt boxes (276 twips, typst pitch-single). docx/njd-complaint.lua writes every paragraph itself: the counsel
     block, the court title, the caption (L.Civ.R. 10.1(b)), the numbered paragraphs (Fed. R. Civ. P. 10(b)), the
     headings, the lettered prayer items, the signature blocks, the L.Civ.R. 11.2 certification on its own page, the
     footer (the page number, centred, its line box ending 0.5 in above the edge: typst footer-descent) and the
     section (letter, 1 in margins; NJD-FORM-001). Twips: 20 x pt. pandoc-from: CommonMark with smart punctuation, as
     typst's cmarker reads the body. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" pandoc-from="commonmark+smart+yaml_metadata_block" size="24" body="552" single="276" indent="720" heading="552" heading-before="0" heading-after="0" footer="720">
</reference>
